%T A402572 2309299912920,99299896255560,5064294709033560,298793387832980040,
%U A402572 20019156984809662680,1421360145921486050280,103759290652268481670440,7116970461355713560041440,505304902756255662762942240
%N A402572 Smallest positive integer m such that exactly n primes p satisfy p*(p+1) divides m.
%C A402572 Let f(m) be the number of primes p such that p*(p+1) divides m. This sequence is the smallest m > 0 such that f(m) = n.
%C A402572 Defined for all n >= 0 since a(0) = 1 and f((prime(n) + 1)!) = n for n > 0.
%F A402572 a(n) <= A402577.
%F A402572 a(n) <= lcm(p, p+1 each for p prime in 2..prime(n)). - _Michael S. Branicky_, Nov 21 2026
%e A402572 a(0) = 1 because no prime p satisfies p*(p+1) | 1.
%e A402572 a(3) = 60 because the qualifying primes are 2, 3 and 5.
%e A402572 a(4) = 660 because the qualifying primes are 2, 3, 5 and 11.
%o A402572 (PARI) a(n) = if(n==0, return(1)); forstep(m=2, +oo, 2, if(sum(i=1, #f=factor(m)[, 1], m%(f[i]+1)==0) == n, return(m)))
%Y A402572 Cf. A126798, A402540, A402577.
%K A402572 nonn,new
%O A402572 0,2
%A A402572 _Nguyen Trong Nhan_, Nov 21 2026
%E A402572 a(12) onward from _Michael S. Branicky_, Nov 21 2026
